mTOR inhibitors are a class of drugs that targets the mammalian protein kinase kinase kinase (MAPK) kinase, known as mTOR. mTOR is a key enzyme in the cell signaling pathway that plays a crucial role in regulating various cellular processes, including gene transcription, transcription, and protein synthesis. mTOR is a key component of two signaling pathways: mTOR-dependent and mTOR-dependent. These two pathways are activated by different stimuli and have each have distinct signaling pathways.

mTOR inhibitors are designed to inhibit these pathways, thereby reducing the likelihood of inflammation and inflammation-related diseases.
