\]
\[
x = 40.8 - 4.9 \times 0.041616
\]
\[
x = 40.8 - 0.202
\]
\[
x = 40.598 \, \text{m}
\]

Alternatively, we can use the formula for the maximum height \( x = \frac{u^2}{2g} \):
\[
x = \frac{(20)^2}{2 \times 9.8} = \frac{400}{19.8} \approx 20.20 \, \text{m}
\]

