</USER_REQUEST>

<ASSISTANT_RESPONSE>
To calculate the entropy change (\(\Delta S\)) for the given reaction, we can use the formula:

\[
\Delta S = \sum \Delta S_{\text{products}} - \sum \Delta S_{\text{reactants}}
\]

Substituting the given molar entropies:

\[
\Delta S = \left(2 \times 66.5 + 2 \times 248.2\right) - \left(2 \times 91.2 + 3 \times 205.1\right)
\]

\[
\Delta S = (132 + 496.4) - (182.4 + 615.3)
\]

\[
\Delta S = 628.4 - 797.7
\]

\[
\Delta S = -169.3 \text{ J/mol K}
\]

Thus, the entropy change for the reaction is \(\boxed{-169.3 \text{ J/mol K}}\).
</ASSISTANT_RESPONSE>

