  \mu = \frac{\text{Force of friction}}{\text{Normal force}}
  \]  
- Since friction and normal forces have units of \([N] = [kg \cdot \text{m/s}^2] = [Mkgm^{-1}s^{-2}]\), the ratio is dimensionless.  
- Therefore, the dimension representation is \( [M^0L^0T^0] \), which means no mass, length, or time.  

