The limit \( \lim_{x \to 0} \tan^{-1}\left(\frac{1}{x}) \), does not exist because the limit does not exist. 

\[ \lim_{x \to 0^+} \tan^{-1}\left(\frac{1}{x}\right) = \frac{\pi}{2}, \]
and
\[ \lim_{x \to 0^-} \tan^{-1}\left(\frac{1}{x}\right) = -\frac{\pi}{2}. \]
