\]

(b) The integral of $3 e^x + 2 \sqrt{x}$ is $3 e^x + 2 \cdot \frac{2}{3} x^{3/2}$.  
\[
\int_{0}^{1} (3 e^x + 2 \sqrt{x}) d x = 3 e^x + \frac{4}{3} x^{3/2} \Big|_0^1 = \left(3 e^1 + \frac{4}{3} 1^{3/2}\right) - \left(3 e^0 + \frac{4}{3} 0^{3/2}\right) = \left(3 e + \frac{4}{3}\right) - (3 + 0) = 3 e + \frac{4}{3} - 3 = 3 e - \frac{5}{3}.
