\[
\nabla F = \frac{\partial F}{\partial x} \hat{i} + \frac{\partial F}{\partial y} \hat{j} + \frac{\partial F}{\partial z} \hat{z} = 2x \hat{i} + 2y \hat{j} + 18z \hat{k}.
\]
At the point \((4,2,-2)\), the gradient is:
\[
\nabla F(4,2,-2) = 2(4) \hat{i} + 2(2) \hat{j} + 18(-2) \hat{k} = 8\hat{i} + 4\hat{j} - 36\hat{k}.
\]
The gradient \(\vec{u} = \langle 8, 4, -36 \rangle\) is the tangent vector to the normal curve at the point \((4,2,-2)\). Thus, the normal curve is given by:
\[

\vec{r}(t) = \langle 4,2,-2 \rangle + t \langle 8,4,-36 \rangle = \langle 4 + 8t, 2 + 4t, -2 - 36t \rangle.
\]
The normal curve is given by:
\[

\begin{cases}
\begin{cases}x = 4 + 8t \\
y = 2 + 4t \\
z = -2 - 36t
\end{cases}
\end{cases
