","(a) The acceleration of the proton is given by the formula \( F = p \times E \), where \( F \) is the force on the proton, \( p \) is the charge of the proton, and \( E \) is the electric field strength. The force on the proton is:  
\[ F = p \times E = (1.60 \times 10^{-19} \, \text{C}) \times (500 \, \text{N/cm}) = 8000 \, \text{N} \]  
The acceleration \( a \) is given by:  
\[ a = \frac{F}{m} = \frac{8000 \, \text{N}}{1.67 \times 10^{-27} \, \text{kg}} = 4.7.8 \times 10^{28} \, \text{m/s}^2 \]  
Thus, the acceleration of the proton is \(\boxed{4.8 \times 10^{28} \, \text{m/s}^2}\).  

(b) The acceleration \( a \) is constant, and the proton starts from rest, so its velocity \( v \) is:  
\[ v = a \times t \]  
Solving for \( t \):  
\[ t = \frac{v}{a} = \frac{35,000 \, \text{m/s}}{4.8 \times 10^{28} \, \text{m/s}^2} = 7.3 \times 10^{-23} \, \text{s} \]  
Thus, it takes \(\boxed{7.3 \times 10^{-23} \, \text{s}}\) for the proton to reach a speed of \(35,000 \, \text{m/s}\).",fluency,"# Task Description
