   \[
   Q_{\text{gas}} = m_{\text{gas}} \times C_p \times \Delta T
   \]
   where \( m_{\text{gas}} \) is the mass of the gas, \( C_p \) is the specific heat of the gas, and \( \Delta T \) is the change in temperature.

2. **Heat absorbed by the water:**
   The heat absorbed by the water is given by:
   \[
   Q_{\text{water}} = L_{\vap} \times m_{\text{gas}}
   \]
   where \( L_{\text{vap}} \) is the latent heat of vaporization of water at 220°C, and \( m_{\text{gas}} \) is the mass of the gas (since all heat from the gas is absorbed by the water).

3. **Equating heat transfer:**
